{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.the-pattern-we-are-modelled-on", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-72ba0ce4f4ea", "line_id": "ln-1eb5eff83cd7", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "What we say is this: you are washed, and you walk in a life made new.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.term.the-flock", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-bdae26e38230", "line_id": "ln-0f76b95f8a7b", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "He is given a people, in one place, and he answers for them.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.confessor-claim-vs-regulated-peace", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-86cc2b81425c", "line_id": "ln-292feefc01db", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "And it still had to be answered by something steadier than one man's word, however real his suffering had been.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.limit.apostolic-origin-undefended", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-fe64e8e319c0", "line_id": "ln-1ba3f4a6a949", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "Cyprian states the principle that carries that line forward.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.grant-me-chastity-but-not-yet", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-5681c74e96e7", "line_id": "ln-209b480edc4d", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "Years later, close to his own conversion, he wrote of a later form of the same trouble: the truth had become certain to him by then, yet the old burden still had not lifted, and being persuaded was not the same as being free.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.the-only-son-and-the-trinity", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-c34da3bc94b3", "line_id": "ln-0958d7fd8ab0", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "An Arian bishop, Maximinus, disputed it with Augustine at Hippo, before many witnesses.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.demo.who-is-jesus-to-us", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-1d1d9ec9cf20", "line_id": "ln-1fd781b2c6e0", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "To us Jesus is the shepherd whose flock this was before it was ever ours to keep.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.violence-commanded-not-cruel", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-3531924649bd", "line_id": "ln-0989c4a3a2c2", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "Our own martyrs entered the kingdom by suffering, not by the sword.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.story.the-death-of-cyprian", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-a926dab6cec7", "line_id": "ln-0f9ab8ae8050", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "Cyprian himself was beheaded on 14 September 258.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.scripture-above-councils", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-0eadbc5d779a", "line_id": "ln-285dca495e90", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "About what it contains, he said, there can be no doubt or argument.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.baptism-traced-to-the-apostles", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-27818b077b80", "line_id": "ln-01a9a8ff0998", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "Two of our practices Augustine traced to the apostles by the same reasoning.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.term.confessor", "kind": "record"}, {"id": "lpc.witness.confessor-claim-vs-regulated-peace", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-5992e9300333", "line_id": "ln-31ea82698128", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "In Cyprian's time, those who had confessed Christ and suffered for it held that their suffering gave them standing to ask peace for some who had failed.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.no-salvation-outside-the-church", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-da9c2ba6c7db", "line_id": "ln-2accf5bdb893", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "We cannot say what he would have held of them.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.baptism-traced-to-the-apostles", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-3c556f5e274f", "line_id": "ln-0b6851de191c", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "That custom, he said, no one could find to have been invented by a later age.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.quote.earlier-councils-corrected-by-later", "kind": "quote"}], "item_id": "gs-80acfb67d207", "line_id": "ln-3376a19a29a7", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "After that came the bishops' own authority, and the councils' own rulings, which could themselves be corrected by later, wider councils.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.heard-for-salvation-not-for-wish", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-d14af43f913d", "line_id": "ln-0b518af49bcf", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "Paul asked God three times to take away a thorn in his flesh.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.limit.ordinary-interior-life", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-3ffc24f9e838", "line_id": "ln-179295ec12e8", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "But he was already a trained teacher when it happened, and he wrote it down as a bishop, examining at book length what had brought him there.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.the-only-son-and-the-trinity", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-958f8b6801c9", "line_id": "ln-0eb0ba19f8d0", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "We confess Jesus Christ, the only Son of God, our Lord.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.quote.bishop-of-bishops", "kind": "quote"}], "item_id": "gs-1c13a61309c7", "line_id": "ln-0769eda244c8", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "Each one judges for himself, and Christ judges him.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.communion-over-separation", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-49c0800f06f0", "line_id": "ln-1ceba489474e", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "He never once put Cyprian outside our communion.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.term.grace", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-aeabd425f1c5", "line_id": "ln-3042f7840246", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "That is what we mean by grace: no effort of ours is enough on its own.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.scripture-above-councils", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-98c3d0bd048b", "line_id": "ln-15d202d329d3", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "About what it contains there can be no doubt or argument.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.limit.womens-own-voice", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-fb5d02de2c43", "line_id": "ln-27731ba6dc7c", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "No text a woman wrote herself survives from us.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.baptism-traced-to-the-apostles", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-4d4e1cefa22f", "line_id": "ln-1f5272418f59", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "He would not rebaptize someone already baptized among heretics.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.gravity.pastoral-office-flock-keeping", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-c553af576257", "line_id": "ln-2068a5a328f7", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "We were held by one office, the office of bishop, and that office was understood as a charge to keep the particular people placed in a man's care.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.limit.ordinary-interior-life", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-e34614d6ccb3", "line_id": "ln-31cb72d424a8", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "Ask us what an ordinary believer felt from inside, and that -- with Augustine's one exception -- is still not ours to give you.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.baptism-traced-to-the-apostles", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-53ab56909d64", "line_id": "ln-0f92be43c03d", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "A custom this old and this universal, with no other explanation for its origin, is rightly believed to have come from the apostles.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.story.celerinus-writes-to-lucian", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-546562c1984a", "line_id": "ln-27f4b945bed3", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "Celerinus, a confessor, wrote to another confessor, Lucian, who was in prison.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.scripture-above-councils", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-efa3f906a590", "line_id": "ln-16c1c81554ed", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "Augustine put it plainly: the canon of Scripture, Old and New Testament, stands far above every later letter of a bishop.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.days-before-the-sun", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-daa3356766a8", "line_id": "ln-1f3b1d9c62f1", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "He named the difficulty rather than explaining it away.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.the-only-son-and-the-trinity", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-f2a86007310e", "line_id": "ln-21d506467129", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "We go on to confess the Holy Ghost as well.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.quote.no-salvation-out-of-the-church", "kind": "quote"}], "item_id": "gs-3913140c560e", "line_id": "ln-2a57d88fd997", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "Even if such a person were killed for confessing the Name, that baptism in his own blood would not help him: \"there is no salvation out of the Church\".", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.the-only-son-and-the-trinity", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-5459cd2c175d", "line_id": "ln-0d5733939bd9", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "This confession did not go unchallenged.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.term.catechesis", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-9e67fcbcd5ba", "line_id": "ln-2c48d7413882", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "You said the creed back, and then we baptized you.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.story.celerinus-writes-to-lucian", "kind": "record"}, {"id": "lpc.witness.peace-for-the-dying-penitent", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-65601533a7d2", "line_id": "ln-2a01de3db8c0", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "Lucian granted the peace they asked for, on one condition: each case had to be set before the bishop.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.limit.ordinary-interior-life", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-fad0ae34ad6f", "line_id": "ln-2ece4fc77363", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "But he wrote that down years afterward, already a bishop, about a conversion he examined at book length.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.confessor-claim-vs-regulated-peace", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-cbddd35456a3", "line_id": "ln-0f9fa6ce707d", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "We took the confessors' claim in earnest, and we also answered it by something steadier: a name set down, then examined before the whole congregation.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.quote.let-your-creed-be-a-mirror", "kind": "quote"}], "item_id": "gs-be1eaad35812", "line_id": "ln-0cc652457d90", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "Augustine told those preparing for baptism to take the creed as a mirror.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.force.decian-persecution-libelli-system", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-37d96eca032f", "line_id": "ln-05a85f7e2780", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "The table was emptied one certificate at a time, and those who remained had to decide what to do with those who came back asking to be received.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.tradition-tested-by-apostolic-warrant", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-b487d5fbef89", "line_id": "ln-29af272fa860", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "Augustine used a different test.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.limit.ordinary-interior-life", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-c48093aa23aa", "line_id": "ln-1432f9dc5a9c", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "How an ordinary day passed for someone sitting in the room, not preaching to it, we cannot tell you from the inside.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.restless-heart-and-the-unrepentant-enemy", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-8a28c5a46d3a", "line_id": "ln-02419361d266", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "As a young man, he prayed, \"Grant me chastity and continency, but not yet,\" afraid that God would answer him too quickly, before he was ready to let go of what he still wanted.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.scripture-above-councils", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-2d8596d977b7", "line_id": "ln-0c0a9dad3595", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "Scripture stood above everything our bishops wrote, and we held it that way.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.communion-over-separation", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-68b149fe33b6", "line_id": "ln-1d0ab95a1626", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "At that same council, he said we judge no one, and reject no one from communion, for thinking differently from us.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.tradition-tested-by-apostolic-warrant", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-7536c02e31e6", "line_id": "ln-25a85160fd61", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "Custom alone, however old, is not enough.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.apostolic-succession-of-boards", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-5b8ab92af9cd", "line_id": "ln-2e16a2a1e94d", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "He stated a principle instead.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.tradition-tested-by-apostolic-warrant", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-434445744ee8", "line_id": "ln-302d5eeaa65b", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "A custom kept everywhere in the Church may fairly be presumed apostolic, even where no apostle's own writing says so.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.term.the-flock", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-320117fc9127", "line_id": "ln-1fb1b4aed404", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "A bishop answered for his flock, and his flock could hold him to it.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.term.catechesis", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-b0d4bad023c4", "line_id": "ln-25d83597988e", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "You were also taught before you were washed.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.restless-heart-and-the-unrepentant-enemy", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-e1b4505cb3dd", "line_id": "ln-147879301590", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "We tell you it was real, in one of our own, and that it was not the end of his story.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.infants-and-the-sin-of-another", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-366b13a06924", "line_id": "ln-25259addd64b", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "We know infants were brought too, and were not made to wait.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.quote.believe-and-thou-hast-eaten-already", "kind": "quote"}], "item_id": "gs-11559e2d1358", "line_id": "ln-1b6009df4c2f", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "He told his people: believe, and you have eaten already.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.term.bishop-of-bishops", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-c44585baa7af", "line_id": "ln-202e829a030c", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "No bishop, he said, makes himself a bishop of bishops.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.quote.earlier-councils-corrected-by-later", "kind": "quote"}], "item_id": "gs-7ee9c9a65e0d", "line_id": "ln-0529907be7a0", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "He wrote:.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.scripture-above-councils", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-70d391515156", "line_id": "ln-0bfef2ebaa83", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "Scripture stood highest.", "world": "lpc"}
{"bindings": [{"id": "lpc.witness.marriage-a-threefold-good", "kind": "record"}], "item_id": "gs-ceada24dac3d", "line_id": "ln-196de45ca44e", "records_commit": "fcd5768412b60ae64e58c639a5624979679bce6f", "sentence": "Augustine named the three goods directly: offspring, faithfulness between the two, and what he called its sacrament.", "world": "lpc"}
